# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. A CRLF shebang line makes the kernel fail to
# recognise `#!`, the script falls back to /bin/sh, and the firewall silently does
# nothing -- the same failure a byte-order mark caused once already. Without this,
# a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true reintroduces it.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF, which is what Windows PowerShell expects.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repo, check out native.
*               text=auto
